# Branch, PR & release guardrails

Read [docs/contributing.md](docs/contributing.md) and [docs/releasing.md](docs/releasing.md) for full detail.

## Branch & git

- Base branch: **`main`**. No direct commits to `main` unless the user explicitly asks.
- Before substantive work: `git checkout main && git pull && git checkout -b feature|fix|docs|chore/...`
- **Never push to `main`** without explicit user approval.
- **Never** run destructive git (`push --force`, `reset --hard`, etc.) unless explicitly asked.
- Commits only when the user asks; otherwise leave changes uncommitted.

## Commits & PRs

- Use Conventional Commits: `feat:`, `fix:`, `docs:`, `refactor:`, `test:`, `chore:`, `ci:`.
- Open PRs with `gh pr create` **only when asked**. Do not merge or approve without explicit approval.
- Prefer squash merge.

## Before claiming code work is done

1. Run **`npm run validate`**.
2. Update tests for behavior changes.
3. Update **`CHANGELOG.md`** `## [Unreleased]` for user-visible changes.
4. Update **`docs/CURRENT_PRODUCT_SURFACE.md`** when routes/endpoints/jobs/integrations change.
5. Never stage secrets (`.env`, credentials).

Trivial docs-only edits may skip validate.

## Releases

- **Manual only** — never run `.github/workflows/release.yml` or create tags/releases unless explicitly asked.
- **Invariant:** `VERSION` = git tag `vX.Y.Z` = GitHub Release `vX.Y.Z`.
- This repo does not publish to npm. Deploy (Vercel) is separate and manual.

## Protected fork customizations

Preserve unless the task says otherwise:

- `AUTH_COOKIE_PREFIX=tgoliveira11-tech`, ports `3011` / `5434`
- `src/proxy.ts` (not `middleware.ts`) for legacy redirects + auth guest pages
- Footer SK → `https://selahkeep.com` in `public-site-config.ts`
